	The following are some suggestions that I have put
	together for 3.1, most of this stuff I have hacked into
	2.3 but haven't gotten into 3.0.
	
	First some comments on current game features...

1) When being transfixed by a floating eye and the eye is then killed
   by your pet you are still transfixed. It would seem that you should
   be released when the eye is killed.

2) When exiting a room all objects which are in the room remain
   visable to you until they are moved (or rot in the case of corpses).
   You then see the object dissappear even though you are in a different
   room.

	Now for the good stuff, some suggestions for 3.1

1) A new object called a compass. When applied the compass would
   point in a direction ("Your compass points SE"), which would
   be the direction of the down stairs in the dungeon levels and
   the up stairs in the case of the maze levels. Various effects
   would be obtained when appling the compass when confused/hallucinating.
   I have this working in 3.0 PL6.

2) Various weapons which require some resource to continue operation.
   Examples would be a light sword which requires batteries (updates
   were posted for this for 2.3 some time back) or a rifle/pistol which
   requires a "box of ammo" to be applied (as on abject) to be reloaded.
   Nasty results might be expected if you are hit with fire while
   carring a box of ammo.

3) Hand Grenades - The was also a post for adding this to 2.3. I modified
   this to make the area affected by the blast proportional to the + factor
   of the grenade and the damage incurred inversely proportional to the
   distance from the grenade. These would also blast out walls and cursed
   grenades could not be dropped after being armed (applied).

4) Wand of petrification - This would turn doors into walls and corredors
   in to stone. Would also turn monsters into statues.

5) A level file similar to a bones file. This file is saved at random times
   when a player goes down a level. The saved file (level.XX) would
   contain everying that was on the level plus a human character 
   (e.g. Barbarian named Ed) which has the Hp AC weapon etc of the player
   at the time. The character would be carring everything that the player
   was carring and the associated attributes of rings amulets etc.
   At the point when the decision is made to enter a bones level
   this level could be used instead. Of course the human character
   would be hostile and would have to be subdued or avoided.

6) Time travel trap - This is a nasty one, a certain points in the
   game the entire game is saved to a special save file. When this
   trap is triggered, the saved game is restored and the player is
   returned to the previous point in time. Everything would be
   exactly as before except that the objects discovered would remain
   known, i.e. the "\" command would not be reset.

7) Worm Hole To Parallel Universe Trap - This would be a variation 
   on the above where the player is returned to a previous point in
   another players game. The player might be allowed to carry objects
   through the worm hole and would remember all discoveries from the
   previous universe.

8) Spell of Control Of Will - This spell would allow the player to
   assume control of a monster. The spell would be very difficult
   to cast (i.e. player must be level > x with so much magic energy)
   and could only be cast by a selected player types.  The success 
   of the spell would also be dependent upon the attributes of the 
   monster. When cast the spell would allow the player to basically
   "play" the controlled monster. The highlight would move from the
   player to the monster and you would see everything that the monster
   sees. Of course, this spell requires such concentration that the
   player (@) could not move or even see the room around him, unless
   the controlled monster can see it. Any disturbance in the area
   of the player (@) would break the spell and return control to the
   player character. The spell could also be broken by the controlled
   monster leaving the level (trap door, etc). The spell would require
   so many energy points per time unit to maintain and could also
   be broken by the monster becoming rebelious.

9) Level of Buildings - This is easy, just let the makelevel code
   create a dungon level and then convert the solid rock and corredor
   types to unlit room. This will yield a level with buildings with
   doors. The only thing to watch out for are the teleport traps
   for vaults. And be sure to leave a boundry of solid rock around
   the whole level.

10) Rooms similar to shops in which you could improve your characters
   abilities, for a price of course. A hospital where you could be
   healed, schools where you could increase you intelligence or
   dexterity, etc. Which you could make use of might be dependent 
   upon your alignment.


